msgid "<0>Kaudu</0> goes after the genitive: <1>Riia kaudu</1>."
msgstr "<0>Kaudu</0> goes after the genitive: <1>Riia kaudu</1>."

msgid "<0>Kaudu</0> takes the genitive: <1>Riia</1>."
msgstr "<0>Kaudu</0> takes the genitive: <1>Riia</1>."

msgid "<0>Läbi metsa</0>, through the forest; <1>üle tee</1>, across the road; <2>mööda teed</2>, along the road: five words for a way, and the case each one takes."
msgstr "<0>Läbi metsa</0>, through the forest; <1>üle tee</1>, across the road; <2>mööda teed</2>, along the road: five words for a way, and the case each one takes."

msgid "<0>Läbi, üle, ümber</0> and <1>kaudu</1> take the genitive: <2>läbi metsa, üle jõe, laua ümber, Riia kaudu</2>."
msgstr "<0>Läbi, üle, ümber</0> and <1>kaudu</1> take the genitive: <2>läbi metsa, üle jõe, laua ümber, Riia kaudu</2>."

msgid "<0>Läbi, üle, ümber</0> and <1>kaudu</1> take the genitive: <2>üle tee</2>. <3>Mööda</3> takes the partitive, from lesson {partitive}: <4>mööda teed</4>. With many nouns the two look different, so the word before tells you which to use."
msgstr "<0>Läbi, üle, ümber</0> and <1>kaudu</1> take the genitive: <2>üle tee</2>. <3>Mööda</3> takes the partitive, from lesson {partitive}: <4>mööda teed</4>. With many nouns the two look different, so the word before tells you which to use."

msgid "<0>Läbi, üle</0> and <1>mööda</1> usually go before the noun; <2>ümber</2> usually goes after it, and <3>kaudu</3> always does."
msgstr "<0>Läbi, üle</0> and <1>mööda</1> usually go before the noun; <2>ümber</2> usually goes after it, and <3>kaudu</3> always does."

msgid "<0>Läbi, üle</0> and <1>mööda</1> usually go before the noun. <2>Ümber</2> usually goes after it, and <3>kaudu</3> always does. Tap the forms to hear them."
msgstr "<0>Läbi, üle</0> and <1>mööda</1> usually go before the noun. <2>Ümber</2> usually goes after it, and <3>kaudu</3> always does. Tap the forms to hear them."

